  "metadata_observations": "All8 lexical endpoints across4 series carry Laterality R; ImageLaterality/FrameLaterality remain blank. One PatientID hash, four per-series frame-of-reference hashes, AcquisitionNumber1 throughout. Series3001 transverse PD fat-suppressed,4001 coronal PD fat-suppressed,5001 coronal T1,6001 sagittal PD fat-suppressed constitute one coherent set. Coronal pair has closely aligned IOP; no duplicated whole protocol or opposing side group. Siemens MAGNETOM Prisma, FFS, blank AcquisitionTime/SeriesTime.",
  "source_header_assessment": "The single unsided report contains a bilateral trochlear wording fragment, while all sampled metadata consistently names the right side and has one acquisition protocol. Headers support a single right-side acquisition candidate, but cannot prove that the bilateral phrase is a typo, history, template material or additional anatomical coverage. It is not a two-report aggregation and is not established dual-knee imaging.",
  "disposition": "single_report_bilateral_wording_unresolved_with_coherent_right_metadata",
  "header_side": "right candidate (raw Laterality R at all8 endpoints)",
  "native_escalation_reason": "No opposing side tags or repeated complete protocol groups materially support a second knee acquisition. Preserve the source wording and ambiguity; no automatic132-image download or clinical-label modification.",
  "native_escalated": false,
  "clinical_target_values_read_or_inferred": false,
  "source_annotation_runtime_files_changed": false,
  "limitations": [
    "All series are represented by exact lexical first/last SOP endpoints, not first/last anatomical slices. Endpoint positions do not establish full volume extent.",
